# Unit Testing

Tests cover robot strategy and simulation logic. Maven wiring stays out of scope.

## Where Tests Live

- JUnit 5 in each module: `robots/src/test/java/` and `simulations/src/test/java/`
- Mirror the main package layout of the code under test
- Keep test types and methods domain-named, matching the robot or simulation they cover

## What to Test

- Robot strategy decisions (when to move, turn, fire, scan)
- Simulation / battle-harness orchestration that contains branching or setup logic

## What Not to Test

- POM files, plugin config, and module wiring
- Trivial getters with no branching
- Robocode engine internals

## Conventions

- Use `org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions` (`assertEquals`, `assertTrue`, and similar)
- Do not add extra assertion libraries unless asked
- Keep tests lecture-simple: `var` is fine; no lambdas unless the user asks
